ategory" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058380/state.json" "file_sha256" "2372dd295512af0f6544be7c4abd582c3f1a36117b84d6c530addae38bce77e1" "basis" 1868 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058380/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-89347" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "t\\in [-\\pi ,-\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\cup (\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058380/state.json" "file_sha256" "2372dd295512af0f6544be7c4abd582c3f1a36117b84d6c530addae38bce77e1" "basis" 1868 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058380/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-89347" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058380/state.json" "file_sha256" "2372dd295512af0f6544be7c4abd582c3f1a36117b84d6c530addae38bce77e1" "basis" 1868 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058380/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-89345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064533/assets/90b505954bb714ad86f60e07f7a26c16c954139689d96684ed553a7b494f0527.png)\n\nOne branch of a hyperbola (shown above) is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $t?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064533/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0300af9b2dd86f38ae9f23a6346439fbb0d70b3965dbb1d5cfe1cc23b047d51" "basis" 2110 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064533/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-89345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a single branch, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064533/assets/b43dcf6c343994e3226e2840a0ae80f60484c8de5d7984f61ec6447185181a76.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0]$ and $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ we get only the right branch.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe only the right branch are\n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=7\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064533/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0300af9b2dd86f38ae9f23a6346439fbb0d70b3965dbb1d5cfe1cc23b047d51" "basis" 2110 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064533/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-89345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064533/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "616afab6d1b3ac2d84eca5bbf5be511c9e5b14d20892c108867c4a49e84dda0e" "basis" 2110 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064533/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-89345" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064533/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0300af9b2dd86f38ae9f23a6346439fbb0d70b3965dbb1d5cfe1cc23b047d51" "basis" 2110 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064533/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-325901" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Complete the following parametric equations generating the hyperbola $2{x}^{2}-8{y}^{2}=16$ in terms of the parameter $t,$ defined for $t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ where $t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\n$x=2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,$\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/state.json" "file_sha256" "636fa6983d58c40e15a33f6aa4ad25de24933f58ddf4e172191689086b10b2f6"} {"question" "q-325901" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The parametric equations of a horizontal hyperbola with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation of our hyperbola in standard form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-8{y}^{2} & =16 \\\\ \\frac{2{x}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{8{y}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have $a=\\sqrt{8}=2\\sqrt{2}$ and $b=\\sqrt{2}.$ Therefore, the parametric equations are\n\n$$\nx=2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/state.json" "file_sha256" "636fa6983d58c40e15a33f6aa4ad25de24933f58ddf4e172191689086b10b2f6"} {"question" "q-325901" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6b79d0c8e71050c67741f67c1d2dde70a5ffeeb2c69963c48f8146b82a95eef1"} {"question" "q-325901" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/state.json" "file_sha256" "636fa6983d58c40e15a33f6aa4ad25de24933f58ddf4e172191689086b10b2f6"} {"question" "q-325901" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{2}\\tan(t)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/state.json" "file_sha256" "636fa6983d58c40e15a33f6aa4ad25de24933f58ddf4e172191689086b10b2f6"} {"question" "q-106509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What are the parametric equations of the hyperbola ${x}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/state.json" "file_sha256" "636fa6983d58c40e15a33f6aa4ad25de24933f58ddf4e172191689086b10b2f6"} {"question" "q-106509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The parametric equations of a horizontal hyperbola with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=1$ and $b=\\sqrt{9}=3.$ Therefore, the parametric equations are\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/state.json" "file_sha256" "636fa6983d58c40e15a33f6aa4ad25de24933f58ddf4e172191689086b10b2f6"} {"question" "q-106509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "v