}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/state.json" "file_sha256" "636fa6983d58c40e15a33f6aa4ad25de24933f58ddf4e172191689086b10b2f6"} {"question" "q-325900" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The parametric equations of a horizontal hyperbola with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation of our hyperbola in standard form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{x}^{2}-9{y}^{2} & =225 \\\\ \\frac{25{x}^{2}}{225}-\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{225} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have $a=\\sqrt{9}=3$ and $b=\\sqrt{25}=5.$ Therefore, the parametric equations are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=5\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/state.json" "file_sha256" "636fa6983d58c40e15a33f6aa4ad25de24933f58ddf4e172191689086b10b2f6"} {"question" "q-325900" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6b79d0c8e71050c67741f67c1d2dde70a5ffeeb2c69963c48f8146b82a95eef1"} {"question" "q-325900" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/state.json" "file_sha256" "636fa6983d58c40e15a33f6aa4ad25de24933f58ddf4e172191689086b10b2f6"} {"question" "q-325900" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5\\tan(t)"] "c