horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(\\pm a,0).$ From the graph, we have that $(\\sqrt{2},0)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nThe asymptotes of a horizontal hyperbola are $y=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}x,$ and so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{b}{a} & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{b}{\\sqrt{2}} & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ b & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/state.json" "file_sha256" "636fa6983d58c40e15a33f6aa4ad25de24933f58ddf4e172191689086b10b2f6"} {"question" "q-106521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6b79d0c8e71050c67741f67c1d2dde70a5ffeeb2c69963c48f8146b82a95eef1"} {"question" "q-106521" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/state.json" "file_sha256" "636fa6983d58c40e15a33f6aa4ad25de24933f58ddf4e172191689086b10b2f6"} {"question" "q-106521" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\,y=\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t"] ["math" "x=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\,y=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t"] ["math" "x=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\,y=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t"] ["math" "x=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t"] ["math" "x=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\,y=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/state.json" "file_sha256" "636fa6983d58c40e15a33f6aa4ad25de24933f58ddf4e172191689086b10b2f6"} {"question" "q-106521" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\,y=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/state.json" "file_sha256" "636fa6983d58c40e15a33f6aa4ad25de24933f58ddf4e172191689086b10b2f6"} {"question" "q-7987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/state.json" "file_sha256" "636fa6983d58c40e15a33f6aa4ad25de24933f58ddf4e172191689086b10b2f6"} {"question" "q-7987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{5}} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{5})^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{5} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{3} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+1 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/state.json" "file_sha256" "636fa6983d58c40e15a33f6aa4ad25de24933f58ddf4e172191689086b10b2f6"} {"question" "q-7987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6b79d0c8e71050c67741f67c1d2dde70a5ffeeb2c69963c48f8146b82a95eef1"} {"question" "q-7987" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/state.json" "file_sha256" "636fa6983d58c40e15a33f6aa4ad25de24933f58ddf4e172191689086b10b2f6"} {"question" "q-7987" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{5}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{5}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}=1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/state.json" "file_sha256" "636fa6983d58c40e15a33f6aa4ad25de24933f58ddf4e172191689086b10b2f6"} {"question" "q-7987" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/state.json" "file_sha256" "636fa6983d58c40e15a33f6aa4ad25de24933f58ddf4e172191689086b10b2f6"} {"question" "q-106526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/state.json" "file_sha256" "636fa6983d58c40e15a33f6aa4ad25de24933f58ddf4e172191689086b10b2f6"} {"question" "q-106526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{3} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{\\sqrt{5}} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{5})^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{5} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}+1 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/state.json" "file_sha256" "636fa6983d58c40e15a33f6aa4ad25de24933f58ddf4e172191689086b10b2f6"} {"question" "q-106526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6b79d0c8e71050c67741f67c1d2dde70a5ffeeb2c69963c48f8146b82a95eef1"} {"question" "q-106526" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/state.json" "file_sha256" "636fa6983d58c40e15a33f6aa4ad25de24933f58ddf4e172191689086b10b2f6"} {"question" "q-106526" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}=1"] ["math" "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}=1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/state.json" "file_sha256" "636fa6983d58c40e15a33f6aa4ad25de24933f58ddf4e172191689086b10b2f6"} {"question" "q-106526" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}=1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/state.json" "file_sha256" "636fa6983d58c40e15a33f6aa4ad25de24933f58ddf4e172191689086b10b2f6"} {"question" "q-325938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=4\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=7\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$=1$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/state.json" "file_sha256" "636fa6983d58c40e15a33f6aa4ad25de24933f58ddf4e172191689086b10b2f6"} {"question" "q-325938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =4\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{4} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =7\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{7} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{7}^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{49} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}+1 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/state.json" "file_sha256" "636fa6983d58c40e15a33f6aa4ad25de24933f58ddf4e172191689086b10b2f6"} {"question" "q-325938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6b79d0c8e71050c67741f67c1d2dde70a5ffeeb2c69963c48f8146b82a95eef1"} {"question" "q-325938" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-ca